@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# Plan
+
+## 1. Tests
+
+- [ ] 1.1 A small SVG referenced from CSS with url() and image-set() is a data URL in dev as in build (playground/assets/__tests__/assets.spec.ts) [AC-1]
+- [ ] 1.2 A small SVG imported from JS is a data URL in dev and keeps the fragment the page appends (playground/assets/__tests__/assets.spec.ts) [AC-2]
+- [ ] 1.3 Editing an inlined SVG sends a new data URL through HMR in the module runner (playground/hmr-ssr/__tests__/hmr-ssr.spec.ts) [AC-3]
+- [ ] 1.4 An SVG excluded by an assetsInlineLimit callback keeps its URL and updates after an edit in the browser (playground/hmr/__tests__/hmr.spec.ts) [AC-4]
+
+## 2. Dev inlining
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Inline an SVG in fileToDevUrl when shouldInline allows it (packages/vite/src/node/plugins/asset.ts)
+- [ ] 2.2 Run the build-only checks of shouldInline only when a build plugin context is passed, and check .html and SVG fragments before the limit (packages/vite/src/node/plugins/asset.ts)
+- [ ] 2.3 Skip the HMR timestamp query for data URLs (packages/vite/src/node/plugins/asset.ts)
+
+## 3. Docs
+
+- [ ] 3.1 Describe the assetsInlineLimit callback return value (packages/vite/src/node/build.ts)
